Package: hyperannotatR
Type: Package
Title: Region-of-Interest Annotation for Hyperspectral Data
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Annotate multiple layers of regions of interest in hyperspectral
    data cubes and their associated display rasters.
    Annotations are stored as validated simple-feature geometries in image pixel
    coordinates with explicit pyramid-level transforms, and can be rasterised to
    binary, labelled, or multi-class integer masks for downstream segmentation and
    classification workflows. A batch annotation application built on 'shiny'
    supports resumable sessions across image queues, live mask preview, and
    export to 'GeoJSON', 'QuPath', and 'TIFF' formats. A versioned partner
    contract exchanges hash-inventoried handoff directories, deep-learning
    training datasets and typed commands over an optional local control
    service.
